WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:02.200
- At President Trump's inauguration,

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:05.020
he spoke of American carnage.

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:07.850
Well, he delivered.

00:00:07.850 --> 00:00:09.770
There is apparently nothing

00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:12.083
that President Trump cannot defile.

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:15.870
As you probably know, a right wing,

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:19.530
Trump-supporting violent mob
breached the U.S. Capitol.

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:21.830
They broke windows, they blew past police,

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:24.820
and they stormed both
chambers of Congress.

00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:26.630
They wore American flags

00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:30.300
and were apparently incapable of irony.

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:34.350
I remember I visited Congress
when I was in high school.

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:39.080
The Capitol is a building
that oozes history.

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:42.140
And unfortunately we
are witnessing a history

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:43.343
of a different kind.

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:46.560
In the Civil War, the Confederates

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:48.470
only made it as far as Fort Sumner.

00:00:48.470 --> 00:00:53.350
Yet today, a Confederate flag
flew inside the U.S. Capitol.

00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:56.037
And today, riders
lowered the American flag

00:00:56.037 --> 00:00:59.940
to instead fly a Trump flag.

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:03.070
And throughout it all, like
Nero playing his fiddle

00:01:03.070 --> 00:01:07.293
while Rome burned, Trump sat
back and watched cable news.

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:12.330
And apparently Trump actually
basks in this mayhem,

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:14.790
saying on Twitter, "These
are the things and events

00:01:14.790 --> 00:01:17.420
that happen when a sacred
landslide election victory

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:20.111
is so unceremoniously and
viciously stripped away

00:01:20.111 --> 00:01:22.420
from great patriots who have been badly

00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:24.920
and unfairly treated for so long."

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:27.300
In reality, this is the most direct attack

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:29.823
on our Capitol since 1814.

00:01:30.710 --> 00:01:33.833
And they have delayed the certification

00:01:33.833 --> 00:01:36.563
of our democratic process.

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:39.580
It's hard for me to even think

00:01:39.580 --> 00:01:43.853
of a worse scenario for our democracy.

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:46.690
The president and his supporters

00:01:46.690 --> 00:01:49.393
have made the United
States a laughingstock.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:54.055
Now, I'll compile my thoughts
and do a full video on

00:01:54.055 --> 00:01:55.640
whether the president and his supporters

00:01:55.640 --> 00:01:59.090
have committed incitement,
sedition, and treason.

00:01:59.090 --> 00:02:01.931
But apart from these legal technicalities,

00:02:01.931 --> 00:02:06.530
we know who was responsible for today.

00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:10.767
As the president was on his
dais, he incited the mob,

00:02:10.767 --> 00:02:12.490
going so far to say,

00:02:12.490 --> 00:02:13.790
- We will never give up,

00:02:13.790 --> 00:02:16.460
we will never concede, it doesn't happen.

00:02:16.460 --> 00:02:18.840
And after this, we're gonna walk down,

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:21.097
and I'll be there with you,
but we're gonna walk down

00:02:21.097 --> 00:02:24.760
to the Capitol
(crowd cheers)

00:02:25.770 --> 00:02:29.660
and we're gonna cheer
on our brave senators

00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:32.510
and congressmen and women.

00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:35.020
And we're probably not
gonna be cheering so much

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:36.990
for some of them.

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:39.080
- Like a wannabe dictator, he said...

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:43.180
- Because you'll never take
back our country with weakness.

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:46.220
You have to show strength
and you have to be strong.

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:48.670
- Similarly, the
president's right-hand man,

00:02:48.670 --> 00:02:51.520
Rudy Giuliani, demanded trial by combat.

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:54.570
- Let's have trial by combat.

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:58.370
- By both incitement and omission,

00:02:58.370 --> 00:03:00.510
this president and his
cronies are responsible

00:03:00.510 --> 00:03:04.510
for what happened today in
one of the worst attacks

00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:08.870
on both our democracy and
the physical buildings

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:11.360
that are the manifestation
of our government,

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:12.780
which are not always the same thing.

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:16.230
But today, life imitates art.

00:03:16.230 --> 00:03:19.500
And they did their damnedest to attack

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:24.270
both the idea of our democracy
and our democracy itself.

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:27.190
The president failed to
deploy the National Guard

00:03:27.190 --> 00:03:29.230
or properly defend the Capitol,

00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:31.030
both before the mob arrived

00:03:31.030 --> 00:03:34.870
and long after it started
to attack the Capitol.

00:03:34.870 --> 00:03:38.790
There's right now talk of
implementing the 25th Amendment,

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:43.130
as if his feckless cabinet
members would actually do it.

00:03:43.130 --> 00:03:45.960
But even if they would,
that's too good for him.

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:49.360
If one thing is certain today,

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:51.720
it's that the president, Donald Trump,

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:54.480
needs to be impeached and removed.

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:58.850
And I can't help but draw an analogy to

00:03:58.850 --> 00:04:02.660
what happened just a few
months ago in Lafayette Square.

00:04:02.660 --> 00:04:05.050
You might recall that
the president attacked

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:08.778
unarmed, peaceful protestors
in a public street

00:04:08.778 --> 00:04:11.460
just so he could get a cynical photo op

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:15.080
in front of a church and
hold a Bible upside down.

00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:18.320
He was willing to employ
every military officer,

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:21.120
every federal employee with a gun

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:23.780
to move aside these people exercising

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:25.330
their first amendment rights

00:04:25.330 --> 00:04:28.430
so that he could get a photo op.

00:04:28.430 --> 00:04:30.480
And it turns out, and I have to admit,

00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:32.670
I did not see this one coming,

00:04:32.670 --> 00:04:34.950
that you can abuse the National Guard

00:04:34.950 --> 00:04:38.800
and the military and the
police by deploying them

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:41.040
and also by withholding them,

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:43.200
which is what the president did today.

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:46.570
In the face of a violent mob
that was armed to the teeth,

00:04:46.570 --> 00:04:48.713
the president turned a blind eye.

00:04:49.630 --> 00:04:51.110
I'm not talking about the people

00:04:51.110 --> 00:04:52.490
who are protesting them at all,

00:04:52.490 --> 00:04:54.420
fine, that's your right.

00:04:54.420 --> 00:04:57.020
We're allowed to disagree with each other.

00:04:57.020 --> 00:05:00.030
But as they turned their
ire that was stoked

00:05:00.030 --> 00:05:01.973
by the president himself,

00:05:03.190 --> 00:05:04.550
the president was okay with it,

00:05:04.550 --> 00:05:07.740
because they were on his team.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:10.330
And there's a famous photo of troops

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:13.080
at the Lincoln Memorial in the summertime

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:17.293
wearing full fatigues, prepared
for just about anything.

00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:21.250
But that wasn't the case today,

00:05:21.250 --> 00:05:23.360
on the day that Congress was supposed

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:27.280
to certify the results of the election.

00:05:27.280 --> 00:05:30.770
Because these riders were
on the president's team.

00:05:30.770 --> 00:05:33.140
They were loved by the president.

00:05:33.140 --> 00:05:36.600
Even as they destroyed the
government, he loved them.

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:40.140
And apart from the complete
lack of preparation,

00:05:40.140 --> 00:05:41.270
there were conflicting reports

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:43.290
about the National Guard being deployed

00:05:43.290 --> 00:05:45.960
at the request of the mayor of D.C.

00:05:45.960 --> 00:05:47.880
and that it's possible that the Department

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:51.550
of Defense refused to allow
the D.C. National Guard

00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:56.180
to protect the Capitol
after it was under siege.

00:05:56.180 --> 00:05:58.170
Eventually, the National
Guard from other states

00:05:58.170 --> 00:06:00.480
were deployed, but it's indisputable that

00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:03.860
even they weren't deployed
except after extreme delay.

00:06:03.860 --> 00:06:07.850
This would be comical if it
wasn't so sad and terrifying.

00:06:07.850 --> 00:06:11.210
It's the stuff of B-movie
schlock like "White House Down,"

00:06:11.210 --> 00:06:13.070
the kind of thing that's popcorn fodder

00:06:13.070 --> 00:06:15.690
because it's so hilariously impossible.

00:06:15.690 --> 00:06:19.303
And yet today in America it happened.

00:06:20.290 --> 00:06:22.670
It didn't take a foreign
military to invade.

00:06:22.670 --> 00:06:26.140
It took Donald Trump's
incompetence and venality.

00:06:26.140 --> 00:06:28.300
We're going to have to have
a full investigation as to

00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:30.870
how a moderately-sized crowd

00:06:30.870 --> 00:06:33.033
could breach the American Capitol.

00:06:34.090 --> 00:06:36.720
But at the moment, video appears to show

00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:39.750
that it's possible that
Capitol or Metropolitan Police

00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:42.900
were complicit in this mob
and allowed riders through

00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:44.100
towards the Capitol.

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:48.320
And eventually, once the mob
breached the Capitol doors,

00:06:48.320 --> 00:06:52.690
some of the cops were taking
selfies with these terrorists.

00:06:52.690 --> 00:06:55.050
And don't tell me that the
Capitol Police are incapable

00:06:55.050 --> 00:06:56.610
of arresting people.

00:06:56.610 --> 00:06:59.130
I've seen Capitol police arrest disabled,

00:06:59.130 --> 00:07:00.830
peaceful protesters before

00:07:00.830 --> 00:07:03.390
and drag them out by their crutches.

00:07:03.390 --> 00:07:06.000
And nationally, 14,000
people were arrested

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:08.320
during the George Floyd protests.

00:07:08.320 --> 00:07:11.810
It seems impossible, but
two incendiary devices,

00:07:11.810 --> 00:07:14.920
probably pipe bombs, were
brought to the Capitol.

00:07:14.920 --> 00:07:17.630
Many of these people were armed.

00:07:17.630 --> 00:07:20.960
However many arrests happen
today, it's not enough.

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:22.650
And let's not forget the senators

00:07:22.650 --> 00:07:25.530
and congresspeople who
promoted this fantasy

00:07:25.530 --> 00:07:27.710
and engaged in these conspiracy theories

00:07:27.710 --> 00:07:31.130
because they thought it
was politically expedient.

00:07:31.130 --> 00:07:33.880
They forgot that words have consequences.

00:07:33.880 --> 00:07:38.120
Senators like Josh Hawley,
Ted Cruz, Ron Johnson,

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:41.280
Kelly Loeffler, James
Lankford, David Purdue,

00:07:41.280 --> 00:07:44.520
Steve Daines, John
Kennedy, Marsha Blackburn,

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:47.850
Mike Braun, Cynthia
Lummis, Roger Marshall,

00:07:47.850 --> 00:07:50.263
Bill Hagerty, and Tommy Tuberville.

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:54.840
Thankfully, some of those
people are no longer senators.

00:07:54.840 --> 00:07:56.170
And good riddance.

00:07:56.170 --> 00:07:57.800
As my friends at "Crew" put it,

00:07:57.800 --> 00:08:01.170
Trump loaded the gun and
Congress pulled the trigger.

00:08:01.170 --> 00:08:03.390
Remarkably, some of these very senators,

00:08:03.390 --> 00:08:05.150
like Senators Hawley and Cruz,

00:08:05.150 --> 00:08:08.820
have actually been fundraising
during the insurrection

00:08:08.820 --> 00:08:13.450
as the mob reportedly rushed
the two chambers of Congress.

00:08:13.450 --> 00:08:16.970
Senator Romney reportedly
excoriated Senator Cruz,

00:08:16.970 --> 00:08:19.480
saying this was his responsibility,

00:08:19.480 --> 00:08:22.080
that he brought this insurrection on.

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:23.670
And he's right.

00:08:23.670 --> 00:08:26.420
I was watching the floor
debate this afternoon.

00:08:26.420 --> 00:08:28.630
In his objection on the
floor of the Senate,

00:08:28.630 --> 00:08:31.010
Senator Cruz cited statistics
about a large number

00:08:31.010 --> 00:08:31.970
of Americans who believed

00:08:31.970 --> 00:08:33.990
in this ridiculous conspiracy theory.

00:08:33.990 --> 00:08:36.360
- I understand your
concerns, but I urge you

00:08:36.360 --> 00:08:40.050
to pause and think, what does it say

00:08:40.050 --> 00:08:42.230
to the nearly half the country

00:08:42.230 --> 00:08:44.290
that believes this election was rigged

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:48.770
if we vote not even to consider the claims

00:08:49.630 --> 00:08:52.720
of illegality and fraud in this election?

00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:54.940
- Which is ironic because a large number

00:08:54.940 --> 00:08:56.870
of people believe it
because people like him

00:08:56.870 --> 00:08:59.320
promoted the ridiculous conspiracy theory.

00:08:59.320 --> 00:09:01.630
Now, Cruz, always a cynical politician,

00:09:01.630 --> 00:09:04.080
implied he didn't believe
it and didn't think

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:05.890
that we should change the
outcome of the election,

00:09:05.890 --> 00:09:09.670
but said, "We should at least
engage in these objections.

00:09:09.670 --> 00:09:11.800
We're just asking questions.

00:09:11.800 --> 00:09:14.510
We can't tell them to jump in a lake."

00:09:14.510 --> 00:09:18.340
Well, with absolutely zero
respect, Senator Cruz,

00:09:18.340 --> 00:09:21.500
these people can jump in a
lake and never come back.

00:09:21.500 --> 00:09:23.680
Riders stormed the
State House in Michigan,

00:09:23.680 --> 00:09:25.370
tried to kidnap the governor,

00:09:25.370 --> 00:09:27.900
and invaded the governor's
house in Kentucky.

00:09:27.900 --> 00:09:29.830
All the while, certain
Republicans continued

00:09:29.830 --> 00:09:31.559
to fan the flames.

00:09:31.559 --> 00:09:34.240
And in the face of an impeachment,

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:36.660
perhaps a stronger case than in Watergate,

00:09:36.660 --> 00:09:38.603
they still played politics.

00:09:39.580 --> 00:09:41.910
At one point, President Trump

00:09:41.910 --> 00:09:44.460
in the debate famously said with regard

00:09:44.460 --> 00:09:46.927
to the racist organization the Proud Boys,

00:09:46.927 --> 00:09:49.260
"Stand back and stand by."

00:09:49.260 --> 00:09:52.740
- Proud boys, stand back and stand by.

00:09:52.740 --> 00:09:55.033
- Well, they did, until today.

00:09:56.010 --> 00:10:00.340
And to those of you who
voted for these politicians,

00:10:00.340 --> 00:10:02.180
you knew damn well that they were snakes

00:10:02.180 --> 00:10:03.710
when you let them in.

00:10:03.710 --> 00:10:06.540
And all while this
insurrection was happening,

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:09.060
the president made it worse, saying,

00:10:09.060 --> 00:10:11.530
- We love you, you're very special.

00:10:11.530 --> 00:10:14.290
- Even as they are literally trying

00:10:14.290 --> 00:10:18.530
to bring down the
government, he can't help

00:10:18.530 --> 00:10:21.690
but praise them because he
thinks they're on his team.

00:10:21.690 --> 00:10:25.050
His attempts to disarm
these people via tweet

00:10:25.050 --> 00:10:27.950
or video were so laughably pathetic

00:10:27.950 --> 00:10:30.890
that Twitter suspended
the president's account

00:10:30.890 --> 00:10:34.030
because they were worried it
was doing more harm than good,

00:10:34.030 --> 00:10:37.400
which is probably exactly
what the president wants.

00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:39.430
He's not going to be president in 14 days,

00:10:39.430 --> 00:10:40.773
so let it all burn.

00:10:41.660 --> 00:10:43.780
If we've learned anything
from this whole affair,

00:10:43.780 --> 00:10:45.420
it's that we absolutely have

00:10:45.420 --> 00:10:49.430
to impeach President Trump
again, remove him from office,

00:10:49.430 --> 00:10:52.620
and prevent him from
taking any office again.

00:10:52.620 --> 00:10:55.620
This is a man who cannot hold power.

00:10:55.620 --> 00:10:57.550
There are 14 days left in this presidency,

00:10:57.550 --> 00:10:59.653
and that's far, far too long.

00:11:00.540 --> 00:11:04.200
Who knows what kind of damage
that he can do in that time?

00:11:04.200 --> 00:11:07.990
And the 25th Amendment, frankly,
is too good for this man.

00:11:07.990 --> 00:11:11.137
At the very least, we can't
let him pardon the traitors

00:11:11.137 --> 00:11:15.240
who invaded the U.S. Capitol,
let alone all of his cronies

00:11:15.240 --> 00:11:18.933
who have done untold number
of illegal and immoral things.

00:11:22.480 --> 00:11:25.327
On the campaign trail,
President Trump said,

00:11:25.327 --> 00:11:26.887
"What do you have to lose?"

00:11:28.280 --> 00:11:31.110
Well, it turns out, everything.

00:11:31.110 --> 00:11:35.030
But we are stronger than this small man.

00:11:35.030 --> 00:11:38.550
We are stronger than this pathetic mob.

00:11:38.550 --> 00:11:40.850
Members of Congress are
working through the night

00:11:40.850 --> 00:11:43.133
to certify the election,
and that's amazing.

00:11:44.460 --> 00:11:45.510
We already voted.

00:11:45.510 --> 00:11:49.373
We sent Donald Trump
packing, and good riddance.

00:11:51.500 --> 00:11:53.840
We're going to rebuild the Capitol.

00:11:53.840 --> 00:11:55.403
It's just a building.

00:11:56.400 --> 00:11:58.850
And this is the last pathetic gasp

00:11:58.850 --> 00:12:01.720
of the failed experiment of Trumpism.

00:12:01.720 --> 00:12:03.823
And again, good riddance.

00:12:04.920 --> 00:12:07.160
And thank you for showing the world

00:12:07.160 --> 00:12:09.823
just how pathetic your movement is,

00:12:10.710 --> 00:12:13.793
how willing to engage in violence you are,

00:12:14.920 --> 00:12:17.910
how all of your criticisms
were in bad faith,

00:12:17.910 --> 00:12:20.430
and how you are the worst of all of us,

00:12:20.430 --> 00:12:22.933
how deplorable you are.

00:12:25.730 --> 00:12:29.343
Your movement will die
an ignominious death.

00:12:30.470 --> 00:12:32.500
And let this be a lesson.

00:12:32.500 --> 00:12:35.570
Being a patriot doesn't mean
wearing an American flag.

00:12:35.570 --> 00:12:37.480
It means standing up for our institutions

00:12:37.480 --> 00:12:39.940
and fighting conspiracy theories.

00:12:39.940 --> 00:12:41.740
So let's unmask these traitors,

00:12:41.740 --> 00:12:44.083
let's ridicule them, let's arrest them.

00:12:45.020 --> 00:12:46.270
And let's start with the one

00:12:46.270 --> 00:12:49.263
that currently lives at 1600 Pennsylvania.

